  "summary": "Afghanistan’s Ministry of Foreign Affairs lists its visa types but does not say which nationalities need a visa; the UK, Canadian and German governments say their citizens need a visa to enter. A visa on arrival at Kabul airport is issued only against an official letter or invitation, and foreign nationals of Afghan origin can enter on an entry permit without a visa. The UK, Canadian and Australian governments advise against all travel; the UK says there is a high risk of British nationals being detained or kidnapped and that it cannot give in-person consular help.",
